  'iec-final-local-election-results-sunday-objections-2026-11-07',
  'Final local election results due Sunday as IEC works through objections',
  'Community', '2026-11-07', 'Cape Town ETC', 'https://www.capetownetc.com/news/iec-recounts-five-wards-as-197-objections-put-provisional-election-results-under-scrutiny/',
  'The Electoral Commission plans to announce final results of the 4 November local elections on Sunday 8 November, after dealing with 197 objections and ordering recounts in five wards.',
  'The Electoral Commission of South Africa (IEC) is due to announce the official results of the 4 November local government elections on Sunday 8 November. Until then, the figures residents have seen are provisional.

IEC chairperson Mosotho Moepya reported that the commission had logged 197 objections as of 15:00 on Saturday. Of these, 54 were dismissed and 8 were withdrawn, while two were considered significant enough to possibly affect outcomes. The commission was still working through the rest. Recounts were ordered in five wards, and party agents are allowed to watch them. Moepya cautioned that an objection does not automatically mean votes were miscounted.

In the Western Cape, provincial electoral officer Michael Hendrickse told a Thursday briefing that results from the province were being captured and audited municipality by municipality, with Cape Town among the last to be finalised. He said complaints and objections must follow the legal route, including an application under Section 65 of the Electoral Act.

Residents who want the confirmed outcome for their ward or municipality should wait for the IEC announcement rather than rely on provisional tallies, since council seat allocations can still change where an objection is upheld.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.capetownetc.com/news/iec-recounts-five-wards-as-197-objections-put-provisional-election-results-under-scrutiny/", "https://novanews.co.za/iec-confirms-official-2026-local-election-results-to-be-announced-on-sunday/", "https://iol.co.za/lge2026/2026-11-05-lge2026-65-of-western-cape-election-results-captured-iec-says/"]',
  'agent'
);
